      "correct_index": 1,
      "explanation": "Correct: B. EASM discovery starts from seed inputs such as known domains, IP ranges and ASNs and continuously discovers related assets; a stale seed keeps the sold range in scope. A is wrong: EASM inventory reflects its seeds and discovered connections, and stale seeds can be removed. C invents a score rule. D is wrong: EASM is outside-in and discovers internet-facing assets regardless of cloud provider.",
