      "explanation": "Correct: C. count() counts rows, so one IP hitting one account ten times looks identical to ten different accounts. dcount(UserPrincipalName) counts distinct accounts, which is what makes this a password-spray pattern. The summarize must come after the time filter; filtering after summarise cannot fix the window. D also uses count() and would fire on brute force against a single account, a different pattern. B filters on time after summarising, so the window is wrong. B uses project, which does not aggregate, so it cannot count distinct accounts at all.",
